caption: Godmath and the Fate of the Sacrificed
setting-component: godmath-and-the-fate-of-the-sacrificed

Use current Godmath as the underlying divine accounting system.

A qualifying Blood Moon death is treated as a sacrifice to Niktul. Niktul receives the victim’s higher soul and the normal Godmath sacrifice reward. The soul is sent to Niktul’s torment afterlife rather than to the afterlife it would otherwise have reached.

Niktul therefore profits twice: immediately from the sacrifice and over the long term from tormenting the captured soul. Blood Marks are a setting-specific rebate of some of that divine profit to the hunter.
